### Two passengers, each with their own bags (.N .N .P .N .P)
POST {{host}}/api/textmessages
Content-Type: application/json

{"message":"BSM\n.V/1LZRH\n.F/LH400/12NOV/JFK/Y\n.N/0220123456001\n.N/0220123457001\n.P/DOE/JOHN\n.N/0220123458001\n.P/ROE/JANE\nENDBSM"}

### Several onward flights
POST {{host}}/api/textmessages
Content-Type: application/json

{"message":"BSM\n.V/1TJFK\n.F/SR101/18APR/JFK/C\n.O/SR1234/18APR/ATL/C\n.O/SR5678/19APR/MIA/C\n.N/0085123457001\nENDBSM"}

### Windows line endings (CRLF)
POST {{host}}/api/textmessages
Content-Type: application/json

{"message":"BSM\r\n.V/1LZRH\r\n.F/LH400/12NOV/JFK/Y\r\n.N/0220123456001\r\n.P/DOE/JOHN\r\nENDBSM"}

### Optional elements BRS does not use: .D .H .K .L .T .C .Y .G .X
POST {{host}}/api/textmessages
Content-Type: application/json

{"message":"BSM\n.V/1LZRH\n.F/LH400/12NOV/JFK/Y\n.N/0220123456001\n.D/HOTC/MARRIOT/07MAY/084502L/HV/VANE79HJT\n.H/T4//16\n.P/DOE/JOHN\n.Y/BXJ2238/GOLD\n.C/CRICKET CLUB\n.L/6Y21AS\n.T/380232\n.K/4F0C03\n.X/SEL\nENDBSM"}

### Invalid optional elements BRS does not use (processed with warnings): bad .X result, bad .L, bad .T
POST {{host}}/api/textmessages
Content-Type: application/json

{"message":"BSM\n.V/1LZRH\n.F/LH400/12NOV/JFK/Y\n.N/0220123456001\n.X/SEL/ZZZ\n.L/AB\n.T/!!\nENDBSM"}

### ============ Examples taken from the IATA text (PROCESSED) ============

### IATA 4.9.2: full BSM with acknowledgement request and encryption (the .X line has a value we do not know, only a warning)
POST {{host}}/api/textmessages
Content-Type: application/json

{"message":"BSM\n.V/1TZRH//6543210014/A/123ABC456Z\n.F/SR101/18APR/JFK/F\n.I/AZ318/18APR/FCO/J\n.N/0085123456003\n.S/Y/3A/C\n.P/SMITH/TOM\n.L/XY1C3P\n.T/321A4C\n.E/RUSH\n.R/VIP\n.X/XRAY\nENDBSM"}

### IATA 4.9.3: delete a record at the local station
POST {{host}}/api/textmessages
Content-Type: application/json

{"message":"BSM\nDEL\n.V/1LZRH////123ABC456Z\n.F/SR101/18APR/JFK/C\n.N/0085123457001\n.S/N\nENDBSM"}

### IATA 4.9.4: delete a record at the transfer station, with an onward flight
POST {{host}}/api/textmessages
Content-Type: application/json

{"message":"BSM\nDEL\n.V/1TJFK////123ABC456Z\n.F/SR101/18APR/JFK/C\n.O/SR1234/18APR/ATL/C\n.N/0085123457001\n.S/N\nENDBSM"}

### IATA 4.9.5: change with exception indicators
POST {{host}}/api/textmessages
Content-Type: application/json

{"message":"BSM\nCHG\n.V/1LZRH////123ABC456Z\n.F/SR101/18APR/JFK/C\n.N/0085123457001\n.S/N\n.E/IROP\n.E/UNAC\n.E/RRTE\n.E/STCK\nENDBSM"}

### IATA 6.9.1: standard offload with acknowledgement request
POST {{host}}/api/textmessages
Content-Type: application/json

{"message":"BUM\n.V/1TLAX//1234567890/A/123ABC456Z\n.F/CX881/15JUN/HKG/Y\n.U/AVE4321SQ/024L/T/Y/HKG\n.N/0131123456001\n.Q/006\n.S/N//N\n.P/WONG/V\n.L/SBJ14X\n.R/CUSTOMS REQUEST\n.X/SEL/XRAY/SECURITY/TRANSFER\nENDBUM"}

### IATA 6.9.4: multiple use of elements (the first bag tag of the printed example has only 12 digits, it is corrected here)
POST {{host}}/api/textmessages
Content-Type: application/json

{"message":"BUM\n.V/1LBBK////123ABC456Z\n.F/QF006/01MAY/SYD/J\n.U/AVE4591QF//M/J/SYD\n.N/0120201610001\n.Q/136\n.P/SAMPRAS/P\n.N/0125020244001\n.N/0125020318001\n.U/AKV2479BA//T/J/SYD\n.N/0125020398001\n.I/JL173/01MAY/NRT\n.Q/009\n.S/N/25A/C/010\n.N/0125020577001\n.O/QF322/02MAY/BRI\n.Q/088\n.S/N/31K/C/101\nENDBUM"}

